  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "A criminal investigation led by Bareskrim Polri is currently underway regarding alleged illegal wiretapping of the Indonesian President. The Witness and Victim Protection Agency (LPSK) has confirmed that six witnesses have formally requested protection as the case proceeds. Government officials, including Tito Karnavian and Bahlil Lahadalia, have issued denials regarding reports of travel bans or personal involvement in the activity. Meanwhile, the National Police Commission (Kompolnas) and other observers have emphasized the necessity for institutional transparency during the inquiry. Some government officials have categorized the act of wiretapping the President as an indicator of treason. Political entities have urged law enforcement to conduct a thorough investigation and hold all responsible parties accountable, as the state addresses the security breach at the highest level of government.",
